{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Puo5B52ubkSYuuRrNNsJe8","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/paper/rebuttal_notes.md:9:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/sections/analysis.tex:16:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/sections/conclusion.tex:4:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/sections/methodology.tex:38:We define $\\nve_t = (v/e)_{\\text{config},t} / (v/e)_{\\text{baseline},t}$, where $v/e$ is the critic's mean imagined value divided by mean evaluation return, and the baseline is the highest-performing seed (exp\\_001, seed~1, 505K steps). We restrict to a \\textbf{35K+ window} to avoid early-training inflation. The $\\nve \\geq 1.5\\times$ threshold achieves 27/29 accuracy (AUROC${=}0.971$, 95\\% CI: 0.904--1.000; Appendix~\\ref{sec:nve_robustness}).\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:114:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:118:\\caption{\\textbf{Task~B1}: Sustained CIVO detection sensitivity analysis ($n_{\\text{pos}}=3$, $n_{\\text{neg}}=7$, $n=10$, $\\text{AUROC}=1.000$). All confidence intervals are two-sided Clopper-Pearson exact binomial ($\\alpha=0.05$). $^\\dagger$Optimal threshold in $(3.78, 4.02]$.}\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:140:\\caption{\\textbf{Task~B2}: Any CIVO detection sensitivity analysis ($n_{\\text{pos}}=4$, $n_{\\text{neg}}=6$, $n=10$, $\\text{AUROC}=0.958$). The single false positive at $\\geq 1.5\\times$ is 008e\\_v3\\_s2 (IRD mechanism, not CIVO). The $1.5\\times$ threshold (highlighted) maximizes F1 while maintaining perfect recall.}\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:161:\\caption{\\textbf{Task~B2 (full evaluation set)}: Any CIVO detection across two environments ($n_{\\text{pos}}=8$, $n_{\\text{neg}}=8$, $n=16$, $\\text{AUROC}=0.969$). Includes Walker Walk (14 configurations) and Cheetah Run (2 configurations).}\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:200:\\caption{NVE ROC curve ($n{=}29$ configurations, AUROC${=}0.971$, 95\\% CI: 0.904--1.000). The preset $\\nve \\geq 1.5\\times$ operating point (star) achieves TPR${=}1.00$, FPR${=}0.12$. The Youden-optimal threshold $\\theta^* = 1.53$ (dashed) coincides with the preset threshold, confirming that the $1.5\\times$ cutoff is statistically principled. Two false positives arise from non-CIVO value overestimation: RAVE anchor pollution and obs-decoder SGS side effects.}\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:232:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:236:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/sections/introduction.tex:6:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/sections/results.tex:67:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/main.aux:167:\\@writefile{lot}{\\contentsline {table}{\\numberline {6}{\\ignorespaces \\textbf  {Task~B1}: Sustained CIVO detection sensitivity analysis ($n_{\\text  {pos}}=3$, $n_{\\text  {neg}}=7$, $n=10$, $\\text  {AUROC}=1.000$). All confidence intervals are two-sided Clopper-Pearson exact binomial ($\\alpha =0.05$). $^\\dagger $Optimal threshold in $(3.78, 4.02]$.}}{13}{table.caption.26}\\protected@file@percent }\ndocs/paper/main.aux:168:\\newlabel{tab:sensitivity_b1}{{6}{13}{\\textbf {Task~B1}: Sustained CIVO detection sensitivity analysis ($n_{\\text {pos}}=3$, $n_{\\text {neg}}=7$, $n=10$, $\\text {AUROC}=1.000$). All confidence intervals are two-sided Clopper-Pearson exact binomial ($\\alpha =0.05$). $^\\dagger $Optimal threshold in $(3.78, 4.02]$}{table.caption.26}{}}\ndocs/paper/main.aux:169:\\@writefile{lot}{\\contentsline {table}{\\numberline {7}{\\ignorespaces \\textbf  {Task~B2}: Any CIVO detection sensitivity analysis ($n_{\\text  {pos}}=4$, $n_{\\text  {neg}}=6$, $n=10$, $\\text  {AUROC}=0.958$). The single false positive at $\\geq 1.5\\times $ is 008e\\_v3\\_s2 (IRD mechanism, not CIVO). The $1.5\\times $ threshold (highlighted) maximizes F1 while maintaining perfect recall.}}{13}{table.caption.27}\\protected@file@percent }\ndocs/paper/main.aux:170:\\newlabel{tab:sensitivity_b2}{{7}{13}{\\textbf {Task~B2}: Any CIVO detection sensitivity analysis ($n_{\\text {pos}}=4$, $n_{\\text {neg}}=6$, $n=10$, $\\text {AUROC}=0.958$). The single false positive at $\\geq 1.5\\times $ is 008e\\_v3\\_s2 (IRD mechanism, not CIVO). The $1.5\\times $ threshold (highlighted) maximizes F1 while maintaining perfect recall}{table.caption.27}{}}\ndocs/paper/main.aux:173:\\@writefile{lot}{\\contentsline {table}{\\numberline {8}{\\ignorespaces \\textbf  {Task~B2 (full evaluation set)}: Any CIVO detection across two environments ($n_{\\text  {pos}}=8$, $n_{\\text  {neg}}=8$, $n=16$, $\\text  {AUROC}=0.969$). Includes Walker Walk (14 configurations) and Cheetah Run (2 configurations).}}{14}{table.caption.28}\\protected@file@percent }\ndocs/paper/main.aux:174:\\newlabel{tab:sensitivity_b2_full}{{8}{14}{\\textbf {Task~B2 (full evaluation set)}: Any CIVO detection across two environments ($n_{\\text {pos}}=8$, $n_{\\text {neg}}=8$, $n=16$, $\\text {AUROC}=0.969$). Includes Walker Walk (14 configurations) and Cheetah Run (2 configurations)}{table.caption.28}{}}\ndocs/paper/main.aux:175:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/main.aux:176:[Omitted long matching line]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01G3NX7j17XMN1tmZ9ZwYabH","session_id":"c17d4e9b-d260-4cdf-87d4-b48964bed707","uuid":"3a7bb1bf-fcd3-4506-bd5a-974793197723","timestamp":"2026-05-20T21:41:41.860Z"}
