{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DNMCF8TH5owX3KBk3zicbP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\\section{Related Work}\n2\t\\label{sec:related_work}\n3\t\n4\t\\paragraph{Temporal abstraction in RL.}\n5\tThe options framework \\citep{sutton1999options}, option-critic \\citep{bacon2017optioncritc}, HAM \\citep{parr1998ham}, and MAXQ \\citep{dietterich2000maxq} formalize temporal abstraction through hierarchical policies. Semi-MDP theory \\citep{bradtke1995smdp} provides the mathematical foundation. Action-repetition methods \\citep{sharma2017figar, biedenkapp2021temporl} achieve simpler temporal abstraction via real transitions. The Dreamer family \\citep{hafner2020dreamerv1, hafner2021dreamerv2, hafner2023dreamerv3, hafner2025dreamerv4} trains policies in imagination at fixed $\\dt{=}1$; hierarchical variants \\citep{gumbsch2024thick, mattes2024hieros, li2025lsimagine} maintain separate dynamics per scale. TAWM \\citep{nhu2025tawm} conditions a world model on $\\dt$ within TD-MPC2 \\citep{hansen2024tdmpc2} and achieves consistent gains; the critical distinction is that MPC re-plans from real states, so model errors do not accumulate into a critic (\\S\\ref{sec:discussion}).\n6\t\n7\t\\paragraph{Value overestimation and model fidelity.}\n8\tMaximization bias \\citep{thrun1993issues} has been addressed by Double Q-learning \\citep{vanhasselt2016double}, TD3 \\citep{fujimoto2018td3}, and ensemble methods \\citep{chen2021redq}; in model-based settings, MBPO \\citep{janner2019mbpo} and MOPO \\citep{yu2020mopo} bound rollout error, while MOReL \\citep{kidambi2020morel} and COMBO \\citep{yu2021combo} penalize model uncertainty. \\citet{lu2018nondelusional} identify delusional bias from policy-class constraints. CIVO is mechanistically distinct: the amplifier is the world model's co-adaptation with a learned temporal embedding, producing systematic reward-prediction bias at $\\dt > 1$. Compounding error in multi-step rollouts \\citep{lambert2020objective, asadi2019combating} exacerbates this bias; decision-aware model learning \\citep{hamrick2021planning} optimizes for planning performance but does not address $\\dt$-conditioned co-adaptation. DreamSmooth \\citep{lee2024dreamsmooth} smooths reward prediction targets but does not address the fidelity gap at $\\dt > 1$. Our TCN intervention relates to training-with-noise \\citep{bishop1995noise} and NoisyNet \\citep{fortunato2018noisynet}; PETS \\citep{chua2018pets} and STEVE \\citep{buckman2018steve} use ensemble disagreement for epistemic uncertainty. TCN's environment-specific dose sensitivity (\\S\\ref{sec:forward_results}) suggests CIVO is a structural vulnerability, not a regularization deficiency. Our factorial diagnostic follows \\citet{henderson2018deep}.\n9\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WdHC5g4HMLVvVb1MARNHJr","session_id":"c17d4e9b-d260-4cdf-87d4-b48964bed707","uuid":"5497cb0a-33b9-4171-9af3-19b504cb55ac","timestamp":"2026-05-20T21:41:47.751Z"}
